  "notes": "COMMON PATTERNS:\nCompound verb from {敷|し}く (to spread, lay) + {詰|つ}める (to pack, fill). The {詰|つ}める component adds the sense of leaving no gaps.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nTransitive verb. The thing being spread takes を, and the surface takes に.\n\nCOMMON OBJECTS:\n- {砂利|じゃり}を{敷|し}き{詰|つ}める - to spread gravel\n- タイルを{敷|し}き{詰|つ}める - to lay tiles\n- {畳|たたみ}を{敷|し}き{詰|つ}める - to cover with tatami\n- {芝生|しばふ}を{敷|し}き{詰|つ}める - to cover with lawn\n- レンガを{敷|し}き{詰|つ}める - to pave with bricks",
